<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gyeongguk daejeon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1485">1485</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as National Code (Joseon)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gyeongguk daejeon, or National Code, was the basic law code of Joseon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. Compilation began under King Sejo, and it was completed and promulgated in 1485 under King Seongjong. Organised in six sections matching the six ministries of government, it set out administration, taxation, ritual, military affairs, punishments and public works, and remained in force for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gyeongguk-daejeon.jpg" alt="Gyeongguk daejeon" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 猫猫的日记本 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gyeongguk_daejeon_in_the_National_Museum_of_Korea_2016-11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
